of them carry the company 'INDIAN' with the Rank cell left empty; forty stand in G Kercheval's company (one CPT, one 1LT, one 2LT, 37 PVT). One hundred and thirty-three carry the regiment 'ODD', which the page's own footnote expands as 'Unassigned Colonel'; the row for ZARLEY, J W leaves that cell empty.","tier":1,"work":"Illinois State Archives Black Hawk War veterans database — the Chicago enrollments"}],"url":"https://genealogytrails.com/ill/cook/blackhawkwar.htm","what_it_does_not_supply":["any date of enrollment beyond the year of the war — the index drops the dates the book prints","any residence, address, lot, trade, age or household","any evidence at all that a man was still in Chicago in 1835: enrolling at a place is presence at that place on that day and nothing more","any woman, and any man who did not enroll","the remarks on service that Whitney's volume carries, which are only obtainable from the Archives by post"],"what_it_supplies":["134 men who demonstrably stood in Chicago in 1832 to enroll for the Black Hawk War, three years before the scene","the rank and company each man enrolled in, and the regiment or brigade he was assigned to","83 names printed WITHOUT a surname comma — the French and Potawatomi forms ('AS KE WITT', 'WAB-ME-MIC', 'BOURBONNOIS, FRANCIS SR' being of the other kind) — which is the part of the town's population this project is least able to recover elsewhere","Gholson Kercheval's company as the commonest single body of Chicago enrollments, which touches a man who signs the 1833 poll list this project already holds"]},"uses":["scene","research"]}
